{"name":"Carpathian Dawn","hex":"#dee3c0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dawn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To begin to brighten with daylight.","To start to appear or become obvious."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The morning twilight period immediately before sunrise.","The rising of the sun."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dawn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carpathian Mountains","blocks":[{"text":"The Carpathian Mountains or Carpathians are a range of mountains forming an arc across Central and Southeast Europe. Roughly 1,500 km (930 mi) long, it is the third-longest European mountain range after the Urals at 2,500 km (1,600 mi) and the Scandinavian Mountains at 1,700 km (1,100 mi). The highest peaks in the Carpathians are in the Tatra Mountains, exceeding 2,600 m (8,500 ft), closely followed by those in the Southern Carpathians in Romania, exceeding 2,550 m (8,370 ft)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Morskie_Oko_in_2020.jpg/330px-Morskie_Oko_in_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carpathian_Mountains"},{"title":"Dawn","blocks":[{"text":"Dawn is the time that marks the beginning of twilight before sunrise. It is recognized by the appearance of indirect daylight being scattered in Earth's atmosphere, when the centre of the Sun's disc has reached 18° below the observer's horizon. This morning twilight period will last until sunrise, when direct daylight outshines the diffused light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Desert_Dawn.jpg/330px-Desert_Dawn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dawn"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Castris_rubris_tabula_peutingeriana1.jpg/500px-Castris_rubris_tabula_peutingeriana1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Castris_rubris_tabula_peutingeriana1.jpg/500px-Castris_rubris_tabula_peutingeriana1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Eastern Carpathians as 'Alpes Bastarnice' on Tabula Peutingeriana","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACastris_rubris_tabula_peutingeriana1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/2_%D0%A1%D1%85%D1%96%D0%B4%D0%BD%D1%96_%D0%B3%D1%83%D1%86%D1%83%D0%BB%D0%B8.jpg/500px-2_%D0%A1%D1%85%D1%96%D0%B4%D0%BD%D1%96_%D0%B3%D1%83%D1%86%D1%83%D0%BB%D0%B8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/2_%D0%A1%D1%85%D1%96%D0%B4%D0%BD%D1%96_%D0%B3%D1%83%D1%86%D1%83%D0%BB%D0%B8.jpg/500px-2_%D0%A1%D1%85%D1%96%D0%B4%D0%BD%D1%96_%D0%B3%D1%83%D1%86%D1%83%D0%BB%D0%B8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hutsul people, living in the Carpathian mountains, c. 1872","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2_%D0%A1%D1%85%D1%96%D0%B4%D0%BD%D1%96_%D0%B3%D1%83%D1%86%D1%83%D0%BB%D0%B8.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Tatry_widok_z_Tarasowek.jpg/500px-Tatry_widok_z_Tarasowek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Tatry_widok_z_Tarasowek.jpg/500px-Tatry_widok_z_Tarasowek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View of Tatry from Bukowina Tatrzańska, Poland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATatry_widok_z_Tarasowek.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Lacul_Bucura%2C_Lacul_Ana_a_Lacul_Bucurelu.jpg/500px-Lacul_Bucura%2C_Lacul_Ana_a_Lacul_Bucurelu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn